  "_approach": "A double-time hi-hat build rather than a snare roll: the closed hat starts on spaced 8ths (bar 1), doubles to a full 16th wall (bar 2), then the open hat joins on every 16th too (bar 3) before the whole hat layer effectively runs at double the perceived rate against a kick that straightens and holds through bar 4, velocity climbing throughout — the 'hats double from 8ths to 16ths' technique Myloops and EDMProd both cite as a build layer distinct from the snare roll.",
